@@ -43,3 +43,12 @@ Start the development server:
 ```sh
 bin/dev
 ```
+
+### Log output
+
+In development every line written to `Rails.logger` is mirrored onto the terminal as well,
+so steps of the import runbook -- for instance `script/library_report.rb`, run with
+`bin/rails runner -e development script/library_report.rb` -- show their output while it is
+being recorded in `log/development.log`. The terminal can be trimmed down (or widened) with
+`TERMINAL_LOG_LEVEL`: one of `debug`, `info`, `warn`, `error` or `fatal`, defaulting to
+`info` so SQL traces stay off-screen. The log file always keeps everything.
